    {
      "id": "be-s8-production-functions-c2",
      "heading": "Three algebraic forms",
      "explanation_md": "The slides give three shapes for F:\n\n- **Linear**: Q = aK + bL. Inputs are **perfect substitutes**: you can swap one for the other at a fixed rate.\n- **Leontief**: Q = min{bK, cL}. Inputs are used in **fixed proportions**: extra of one input is useless without more of the other.\n- **Cobb-Douglas**: Q = K^a L^b. Inputs have **a degree of substitutability**: you can swap them, but not perfectly.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Linear production function",
          "meaning": "Q = aK + bL, inputs are perfect substitutes",
          "source_ref": "be--session-8#4"
        },
        {
          "term": "Leontief production function",
          "meaning": "Q = min{bK, cL}, inputs used in fixed proportions",
          "source_ref": "be--session-8#4"
        },
        {
          "term": "Cobb-Douglas production function",
          "meaning": "Q = K^a L^b, inputs have a degree of substitutability",
          "source_ref": "be--session-8#4"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "Linear: perfect substitutes. Leontief: fixed proportions. Cobb-Douglas: a degree of substitutability.",
      "clarification": null,
