    {
      "id": "be-s8-production-functions-c3",
      "heading": "Worked question: a Leontief firm",
      "explanation_md": "The firm's production function is **Q = min{3K, 4L}**, with K = 5 and L = 2.\n\n| Term | Working | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3K | 3 x 5 | 15 |\n| 4L | 4 x 2 | 8 |\n| Q | min{15, 8} | **8** |\n\nWith fixed proportions, output is set by the **smaller** term. Here labour holds output to 8, so the extra capital adds nothing.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-leontief-3k-4l"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "For a Leontief function, work out each term and take the minimum: Q = min{15, 8} = 8.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s8-production-functions-q-4cff0a23",
          "type": "mcq",
          "stem": "Q = min{3K, 4L}. With K = 5 and L = 2, output is:",
          "options": [
            "8",
            "15",
            "23"
          ],
          "answer": "8",
          "accept": [],
          "explanation": "3K = 15 and 4L = 8; a Leontief firm produces the smaller of the two.",
