    {
      "id": "be-s8-production-functions-q-86dc0e63",
      "type": "short",
      "stem": "A firm's production function is Q = min{3K, 4L}. Calculate output when K = 5 and L = 2.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "This is a **Leontief** production function, so inputs are used in fixed proportions and output is the smaller term.\n\n- 3K = 3 x 5 = 15\n- 4L = 4 x 2 = 8\n- Q = min{15, 8} = **8**\n\nLabour is the binding input here.",
